  "post_stream": {
    "posts": [
      {
        "id": 14640,
        "name": "broccoli",
        "username": "broccoli",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/broccoli/{size}/1861_2.png",
        "created_at": "2016-02-25T19:18:11.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>First off, I'd like to say that I love this game, and I play it a LOT. &nbsp;However, there is one thing about the game that annoys me from time to time, and that's when you have an AE where order matters or you have to select X from a set of Y, or similar selections. &nbsp;Firstly, it's tedious, and secondly, on my tablet, the load time to pull back that bar of choices every time can really slow things down.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>As a result, what I would like is something where when you get a choice like this, have the normal \"bar\" with all the cards in it, and then just place an empty \"bar\" above it. &nbsp;Then you could just drag all the individual cards from the bottom bar to the top bar in an order of your choice, and then it would execute left-to-right through that bar. &nbsp;Obviously, it would still process all the individual pieces (increase/decrease for twist the ether, reactions on destroy, etc) for each target, but you would never have to return back to that target selection screen again.</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:46:47.318Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 1,
